.TH HOMEBREWCONFIG 1 "2026-06-15" "homebrewconfig 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
homebrewconfig \- configure Homebrew environment variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homebrewconfig
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homebrewconfig
edits the Homebrew environment variables in your shell profile, either through
an interactive terminal UI or, when a batch flag is given, non-interactively for
scripting.
.PP
With no batch flag, the interactive TUI launches. The tool writes a delimited,
idempotent block to your shell profile (auto-detected from
.BR $SHELL ),
backs up the previous version to
.IR <profile>.bak ,
and leaves the rest of the file untouched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-profile " PATH"
Write to this shell profile instead of the auto-detected one.
.TP
.BI \-\-set " VAR=VALUE"
Set a Homebrew variable (repeatable; runs non-interactively).
.TP
.BI \-\-unset " VAR"
Reset a variable to its Homebrew default (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-import\-preset " PATH"
Load settings from a TOML preset, used as a baseline.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-preset " PATH"
Write the current non-default settings to a TOML preset.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Write the profile without opening the UI.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the export block that would be written, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print all settings and their current values, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the full state as JSON, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
Inside the TUI:
.TP
.BR \[ua] / \[da] ", " k / j
Move the selection.
.TP
.B /
Filter settings by name, variable, category or description.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle a boolean setting.
.TP
.B Enter
Edit a string or number setting.
.TP
.B a
Apply all changes (shows a confirmation and preview first).
.TP
.B r
Reset to current environment values.
.TP
.B p
Cycle the target shell profile.
.TP
.B ?
Toggle help.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview the block that would be written:
.PP
.RS
.EX
homebrewconfig \-\-set HOMEBREW_NO_ANALYTICS=1 \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Apply changes straight to the profile:
.PP
.RS
.EX
homebrewconfig \-\-set HOMEBREW_NO_ANALYTICS=1 \-\-apply
.EE
.RE
.PP
Share a configuration between machines:
.PP
.RS
.EX
homebrewconfig \-\-export\-preset team.toml
homebrewconfig \-\-import\-preset team.toml \-\-apply
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.zprofile ", " ~/.zshrc ", " ~/.bash_profile ", " ~/.bashrc ", " ~/.config/fish/config.fish
Candidate shell profiles, depending on the detected shell.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Vincent Lauriat.
